## Sprint 1 - Windows Server Deployment

### Objective
Build the first virtual machine for the Enterprise Blue Team Lab.

### Tasks Completed
- Enabled AMD-V virtualization in BIOS.
- Verified virtualization support in Windows.
- Installed VMware Workstation Pro.
- Downloaded Windows Server 2022 Evaluation.
- Created the first Windows Server virtual machine.
- Resolved UEFI boot issues.
- Successfully started Windows Server installation.

### Challenges
The VM initially attempted PXE network boot because the UEFI firmware had not yet detected the mounted installation media.

### Resolution
Verified the ISO configuration and allowed the virtual DVD additional time to initialize during boot.

### Lessons Learned
- Modern virtual machines use UEFI firmware.
- UEFI attempts multiple boot devices before launching the installer.
- Enterprise virtualization requires careful configuration before deployment.

### Next Sprint
Complete Windows Server installation and configure the server for Active Directory.
